.TH EVENTFD 3
.SH NAME
eventfd \- libc wrapper for a native event counter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <unistd.h>
.sp
.BI "int eventfd(unsigned int initial_value, int flags);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Astia libc wrapper submits the native event-counter operation to the
process I/O ring and translates negative kernel errors to -1 and errno.
The returned descriptor follows normal close, dup, fork, exec, read, write,
and poll lifetime rules.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a descriptor on success, or -1 with errno on failure.
